1. Modify the setting in run.sh
2. Then execute run.sh: bash run.sh > log
3. After finish the running, check critical timing results in "sum.dat", "sum.dat.ncpu", ...
4. Execute "clean.sh" will delete all outputs in each example and the created files during running  
5. catch_properties.sh is used to catch the energy/force/stress information and write them to a 
   new file. 
   usage: cd EXAMPLE_FOLDER ; bash ../catch_properties.sh result.out
6. sumdat.sh is used to summarize the timing informations of examples in 'allcase' to a new file 'sum.dat'.
   usage: bash sumdat.sh allcase sum.dat

Neighbor-search Phase 4 benchmark
---------------------------------

`neighbor_phase4_benchmark.py` runs the standalone Half14/Full27 probe, the
beta.1 legacy/current Full27/current Half14 grid-path comparison, the
single-node MPI scaling probe, and an optional beta.1/current ABACUS
comparison. Keep the two ABACUS executables and the beta.1 legacy grid-path
probe in separate Release build directories and use the same compiler and
dependency environment.

Example:

```bash
conda run -n bxcx python tests/performance/neighbor_phase4_benchmark.py \
  --current-repo . \
  --beta-repo /path/to/abacus-3.11.0-beta.1 \
  --output /tmp/neighbor-phase4-results \
  --sections grid kernel mpi version \
  --current-grid-kernel /path/to/current/MODULE_CELL_NEIGHBOR_grid_path_benchmark \
  --beta-grid-kernel /path/to/beta1/MODULE_CELL_NEIGHBOR_grid_path_benchmark \
  --kernel /path/to/MODULE_CELL_NEIGHBOR_benchmark \
  --mpi-kernel /path/to/MODULE_CELL_NEIGHBOR_mpi_benchmark \
  --current-abacus /path/to/current/abacus_basic_para \
  --beta-abacus /path/to/beta1/abacus_basic_para
```

Generate the Markdown report with:

```bash
python3 tests/performance/neighbor_phase4_report.py \
  --results /tmp/neighbor-phase4-results \
  --output /tmp/neighbor-phase4-results/Phase_4_Benchmark.md
```

The beta.1 LCAO comparison selects the serial LAPACK solver for one-rank runs.
This avoids an ABI incompatibility between the current conda ScaLAPACK and the
older beta.1 executable. MPI scaling is measured by the dedicated neighbor
probe and must be run outside restricted sandboxes that block PMIx sockets.

The beta.1 grid-path probe compiles the same
`source/source_cell/module_neighbor/test/grid_path_benchmark.cpp` source in a
temporary beta.1 worktree with `NEIGHBOR_BENCHMARK_BETA1` defined. The original
beta.1 Grid has an O(N^2) full-scan path, so large beta.1 cases should be
bounded with `--beta-grid-max-atoms`.
